HHIISSTTOORRYY
     The lliisstteenn() system call appeared in 4.2BSD.  The ability to configure
     the maximum _b_a_c_k_l_o_g at run-time, and to use a negative _b_a_c_k_l_o_g to request
     the maximum allowable value, was introduced in FreeBSD 2.2.  The
     _k_e_r_n_._i_p_c_._s_o_m_a_x_c_o_n_n sysctl(3) has been replaced with
     _k_e_r_n_._i_p_c_._s_o_a_c_c_e_p_t_q_u_e_u_e in FreeBSD 10.0 to prevent confusion about its ac‐
     tual functionality.  The original sysctl(3) _k_e_r_n_._i_p_c_._s_o_m_a_x_c_o_n_n is still
     available but hidden from a sysctl(3) -a output so that existing applica‐
     tions and scripts continue to work.

